Add key events for IR remote controls of digital TV receivers

Maps the evdev codes a receiver remote sends - KEY_RECORD, KEY_EXIT, KEY_OK,
KEY_INFO, KEY_EPG, the colour keys and so on - onto SDL scancodes, which SDL
otherwise reports as SDL_SCANCODE_UNKNOWN.

Originally written by Marc Serdeliuc for SDL 2.0.8 and rebased onto 2.32.x.
The new scancodes are appended at 291 so the values SDL assigns itself stay
untouched, and the three renames the original carried (SDLK_AUDIOPLAY to
SDLK_PLAYPAUSE and friends) are dropped - SDL maps KEY_PLAYPAUSE, KEY_REWIND
and KEY_FASTFORWARD correctly on its own now.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-alliance specific]

